          "run": "1",
          "file": "mlflow/store/tracking/sqlalchemy_store.py",
          "line": 1043,
          "severity": null,
          "message": "Pagination loop: With `max_results=0`, the query uses `limit(1)`. If at least one metric exists, `len(metrics) == max_results + 1` holds. The store then returns an empty list plus a token for `offset + 0`, which is the same offset that was requested. A client that follows `next_page_token` gets the same empty page and the same token forever. The Java `getMetricHistory` `while (!token.isEmpty())` loop is one such client. `max_results` is also not validated, so negative values reach `limit()` as zero or negative numbers. Reject `max_results <= 0` (or treat 0 as \"no limit\"), or skip emitting a token when no rows are returned."
        },
        {
          "case": "unset-proto-field-treated-as-zero",
          "run": "1",
          "file": "mlflow/store/tracking/file_store.py",
          "line": 894,
          "severity": null,
          "message": "Same zero-size issue: `SearchUtils.paginate(all_metrics, page_token, 0)` can likewise return an empty page with a non-advancing next token. This depends on `paginate` emitting a token whenever more items remain. Combined with an unset proto `max_results` arriving as `0`, REST clients backed by FileStore could loop forever or receive empty histories. Validate that `max_results` is a positive integer before paginating."
